/bin/
# Without the trailing slash, so a symlink is ignored too.
#
# A git worktree has no third_party of its own, since the libghostty archive is built rather than
# committed, and linking to the main checkout is the cheap way to make a cgo build work there. With
# `/third_party/` that symlink is not ignored and gets committed by an `add -A`.
/third_party
mise.local.toml

# Zig's build cache. mise's libghostty task builds inside third_party, which is already ignored, but
# setup-zig in CI points ZIG_LOCAL_CACHE_DIR at the repo root. An untracked directory there makes the
# Go build stamp vcs.modified=true, so every release binary reported its version with a "-dirty"
# suffix while the checkout was in fact clean. Caught by reading the version off a published artifact.
.zig-cache/
